title: Integrating is containing; dismissing is hiding.
pid: 7c0abbe1-6c43-4e61-aed0-79ee910fe36f
body: |2-
  To take an unintegrated child, move it into the fork's content; to
  dismiss it, delete it from the subscribee as such, which records a
  hide. Both write the fork's file. There is no third answer, "seen;
  leave it where it is". Writing in a child takes it too (below).
contains:
